❯ Explain in two sentences what a fixed-layout terminal is.

⏺ A fixed-layout terminal is a terminal emulator or interface whose display area has a set number of rows and columns
  (or fixed pixel dimensions) that doesn't dynamically resize or reflow to fit varying content or window sizes. This
  makes it well-suited for applications like TUIs, old-school BBS systems, or games that rely on precise, predictable
  character positioning rather than responsive text wrapping.

